  "text": "Recipe: Black Bean Burgers\nCreator: Vinoo Tahim\nCategory: Burger\nIngredients: rolled oats, corn, black beans, onion, garlic, carrots, beets, low sodium soy sauce, garlic powder, cumin powder, coriander powder, red chili powder, salt, pepper, cayenne pepper, quick oats\nCooking methods: saute, no-cook, freeze, pan-fry\nInstructions: Veggie Masala: Heat a pan. Combine onion, garlic, salt & pepper. Cook until onion is translucent. Add carrots, beets, cumin powder, coriander powder, chili powder & cayenne pepper until carrots are tender. Remove pan from stovetop.\nIn a bowl, mash cooked black beans. Add Veggie Masala, along with soy sauce, quick oats & corn. Mix well & form patties.\nPlace patties in freezer for 30 minutes to set. Then cook them on a pan over medium heat, flipping halfway to cook both sides.\nUse patties to create your dream veggie burger!\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (corn, quick oats), BEANS (black beans), RAINBOW VEGGIES (carrots, beets, onion, garlic), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
